Yes.

278
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:28,080
Absolutely amazing.

279
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,000
Nai is pedaling.

280
00:10:36,173 --> 00:10:36,680
(Uncle Sock is far behind)

281
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:37,760
Wait for Naiwen.

282
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:42,840
♪The little boat drifts gently♪

283
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:47,040
♪On the water♪

284
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:48,560
Alone.

285
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:49,760
(Gliding on the water,
stealing a moment of peace)

286
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,600
It's quite pleasant.

287
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,520
Nai, are you tired?

288
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:55,440
No.

289
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:59,600
He looks relaxed

290
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,360
but is actually worn out.

291
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,480
His pedaling feet
are practically sparking.

292
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,200
Come on, let's race.

293
00:11:06,549 --> 00:11:09,454
(Pure foot power)

294
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,080
I can keep going.

295
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:17,240
You are pretty fast.

296
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:20,280
I can hear

297
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,800
the furious pedaling sounds
coming from behind me.

298
00:11:23,102 --> 00:11:24,791
(Captain Naiwen is sailing over)

299
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,296
It turned out to be Li Naiwen.

300
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:31,200
Clatter-clatter.

301
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:33,800
Hustling away.

302
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,440
This feels so great.

303
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,360
Really.

304
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:43,320
Never experienced this before.

305
00:11:44,320 --> 00:11:46,080
It's really beautiful.

306
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:48,200
You can't help but exclaim.

307
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:56,040
Friends up on the bridge,
how is it going?

308
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:58,600
Time to head back.

309
00:11:59,520 --> 00:11:59,920
Okay.

310
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:01,920
Experience done.

311
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:03,560
Getting ashore.

312
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:06,480
Farewell, mountains.

313
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:09,600
Let's go.

314
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:17,880
Today we've experienced

315
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:20,560
the art and energy of South France.

316
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:22,760
Through the Earth Group's
classic mission,

317
00:12:22,760 --> 00:12:23,800
Circle-Covering Dance,

318
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,400
(Circle-Covering Dance returns)
let's show

319
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,760
our passion and energy.

320
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,600
This is a game

321
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:29,600
we play all the time.

322
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,760
Except for Fei, Chaoyue, and Kai,

323
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:32,920
everyone knows the rules.

324
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,080
(Guo Jingfei)
I know.

325
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,040
Don't include me, okay?

326
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,360
Then explain it to them.

327
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:38,960
Today,

328
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,720
(I actually do know)
our game is four-versus-four.

329
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:42,840
We'll split into two teams.

330
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:45,240
Then one person has a hole on them.

331
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,000
(Deng Kai)

332
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,760
We need to find a way to cover the hole

333
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:50,120
so the other team can't find who has it.

334
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:52,280
We also need to do the dance moves.

335
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:53,240
Pretend you have the hole on you.

336
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,600
You have to do your best
to cooperate with

337
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,200
whatever the opponents
ask you to perform.

338
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:56,880
(The observation team scores if they guess
who has the hole. Otherwise, the hole-covering team wins)

339
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:57,280
How about it?

340
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:57,960
Right.

341
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,760
- Very clever.
- Really.

342
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,160
Two ladies, pick your players.

343
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:03,800
Rock, paper, scissors.

344
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:04,751
Paper.

345
00:13:04,751 --> 00:13:05,702
(First pick)

346
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:07,960
I pick Deng Kai.

347
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,015
Honglei.

348
00:13:10,560 --> 00:13:11,120
Nai.

349
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:13,880
No.

350
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,360
Xingxu.

351
00:13:14,530 --> 00:13:15,599
(Wang Yuwen's team: Wang Yuwen,
Deng Kai, Sun Honglei, Chen Xingxu)

352
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:17,040
I got sent back.

353
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:17,880
I got sent back.

354
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,120
You got sent back.

355
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,120
She regretted picking you, doesn't she?

356
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,680
I was thinking you two shouldn't
be on the same team.

357
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:23,600
Right, so I sent him back.

358
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,040
Did you pay the handling fee?

359
00:13:25,570 --> 00:13:26,628
(Never you mind)

360
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,040
Go over there.

361
00:13:27,152 --> 00:13:28,400
(Circle-Covering Dance teams)

362
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:29,040
- Alright.
- Go over there.

363
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,255
Which team goes first?

364
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,400
Let them go first.

365
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:34,640
Okay.

366
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,080
- Come on.
- Come on.

367
00:13:36,269 --> 00:13:38,117
(Yang Chaoyue's team goes first)

368
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,200
Move to the side.

369
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:41,580
Move a little to the side.

370
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,680
These people are all smart.

371
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,800
They often do the exact opposite.

372
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,440
We do the opposite of their opposite.

373
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,240
Okay.

374
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:50,720
Put it on you.

375
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,000
Okay.

376
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:52,400
Okay.

377
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,422
They'll most likely pick me.

378
00:13:53,422 --> 00:13:54,000
I'm telling you.

379
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:54,280
Really?

380
00:13:55,160 --> 00:13:56,778
We are all suspects.

381
00:13:56,778 --> 00:13:58,480
The three of us together
have an advantage,

382
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,400
but we just can't put it on Chaoyue.

383
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:02,280
Is it possible to put it on Chaoyue?

384
00:14:02,389 --> 00:14:02,840
(Just going for the opposite)

385
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,600
I got your reverse thinking logic.

386
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:04,800
Right.

387
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,679
- If we put it on her...
- You've covered all the bases.

388
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,200
But Chaoyue might get flustered.

389
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,200
He'll be able to tell.

390
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:11,440
Yeah.

391
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,640
Okay, give it to me.

392
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,520
Chaoyue, remember,

393
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:14,560
you have one on you.

394
00:14:14,679 --> 00:14:15,280
(Building up the conviction)

395
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:15,600
Okay.

396
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,840
Just play it like this.

397
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:17,240
Right.

398
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,880
We'll put one on the shoulder,
and the other one down below.

399
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,996
- One up, one down. Easier to handle.
- Okay.

400
00:14:20,996 --> 00:14:21,455
Okay.

401
00:14:24,059 --> 00:14:25,720
(Sticker positions:
Liu Yuning's left shoulder)

402
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:26,760
Like this.

403
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,120
Come on.

404
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:30,123
(Hider: Liu Yuning)

405
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:32,240
One-on-one surveillance?

406
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:33,080
Okay.

407
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,280
I'll keep an eye on Naiwen.

408
00:14:35,328 --> 00:14:37,027
(Circle-Covering Dance, Round 1)

409
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:37,760
Old school.

410
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,360
Fei.

411
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,200
Nice.

412
00:15:22,013 --> 00:15:23,753
(Loosen, loosen)

413
00:15:25,366 --> 00:15:26,531
(Crazy provocation)

414
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:28,120
Nothing at all.

415
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:30,005
(They saw everything?)

416
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,570
- Nothing there. Still wiggling around.
- No.

417
00:15:33,521 --> 00:15:34,419
(Empty)

418
00:15:35,915 --> 00:15:38,074
(Empty)

419
00:15:38,363 --> 00:15:40,073
(Target range precisely narrowed)

420
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:41,240
Eliminate one.

421
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,000
Too excited.

422
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,440
You're too excited.

423
00:15:44,615 --> 00:15:46,154
(Just laying the cards out in the open)

424
00:15:47,757 --> 00:15:48,400
(Please give the prompt)

425
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:49,320
Okay.

426
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:53,640
(Wang Yuwen's designated move: Three ballet spins)
Spin three times.

427
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:54,360
I'll go first.

428
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,612
(Guo Jingfei solo)
Someone needs to block you here.

429
00:15:55,612 --> 00:15:56,120
Right.

430
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,120
So he has to stand

431
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,200
- opposite you.
- Come on.

432
00:15:58,440 --> 00:16:00,400
See if their position is still correct.

433
00:16:00,720 --> 00:16:01,320
Okay.

434
00:16:01,993 --> 00:16:02,440
Go.

435
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:03,318
Go. Okay.

436
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:05,200
Wait a moment.

437
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,480
(Air-tight)
No, wait.

438
00:16:07,807 --> 00:16:10,949
(Guarding)

439
00:16:12,659 --> 00:16:15,245
(Flickering in and out)

440
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,080
Pull up your pants, Jingfei.

441
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,440
Pull up your pants.

442
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:19,920
(Elegant)
Pull up your pants first.

443
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:20,640
Mine?

444
00:16:20,640 --> 00:16:21,280
Pull up your pants first.

445
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:27,960
Guide me. I'll do it.

446
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:30,838
Grab yourself first.

447
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:31,480
Okay.

448
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:31,840
Okay.

449
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:32,840
What is this?

450
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:33,320
Okay.

451
00:16:35,397 --> 00:16:37,144
(Emergency shielding)

452
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:38,880
Block a little.

453
00:16:39,174 --> 00:16:40,179
(Trying hard)

454
00:16:40,352 --> 00:16:40,880
(Trying hard to cover)

455
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:41,640
Block behind me.

456
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:43,600
(Panic)
No, block in the middle!

457
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:46,480
Why are you panicking?

458
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,040
Yeah.

459
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:48,440
It's not on you. Why panic?

460
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,320
(I'm panicking even if it's on you)

461
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,000
Where?

462
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:50,880
Where to block?

463
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:53,720
Chaoyue.

464
00:16:54,158 --> 00:16:55,548
(Arousing suspicion)

465
00:16:55,920 --> 00:16:56,320
Okay.

466
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:58,120
Let's go.

467
00:17:02,611 --> 00:17:03,798
(Key focus on Yuning)

468
00:17:09,719 --> 00:17:11,782
(I'll block)

469
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:14,000
Yuning's lower hand might be it.

470
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,248
We need to make it harder.

471
00:17:18,248 --> 00:17:19,520
(Increase difficulty)
Really challenge them.

472
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:20,640
It's okay.

473
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:22,319
Whatever you come up with, we'll do.

474
00:17:22,319 --> 00:17:22,920
Just like this.

475
00:17:25,599 --> 00:17:26,040
And then

476
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:27,319
shoot.

477
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:34,960
Go easy on yourselves for now.

478
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,560
We might come at you even harder later.

479
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:37,400
Yuning, come on.

480
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:38,760
(Verify Liu Yuning again)
Behind me. Come on.

481
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:39,238
Come on.

482
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:40,520
Nai, grab below.

483
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:41,160
Come on.

484
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:42,080
Okay.

485
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,200
I'll count.

486
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,840
One, two, three. Jump on three, okay?

487
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,160
One,

488
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:50,160
two,

489
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:51,080
three.

490
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,000
Go.

491
00:17:52,560 --> 00:17:53,080
(Can't go)
One,

492
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:54,000
two,

493
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:55,000
three.

494
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:55,520
Wait!

495
00:17:55,520 --> 00:17:55,920
Go.

496
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:56,480
Wait.

497
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,000
One.

498
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,760
Someone's holding me. I can't jump.

499
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,880
No, I'll jump with you.

500
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,120
- One, two, three, jump.
- One, two, three, jump.

501
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:04,560
Three.

502
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:06,160
Go.

503
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:07,240
That hurt so much.

504
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:09,280
It's okay. Do it again.

505
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:11,240
One, two, three, go.

506
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,400
I think it's more likely to be Yuning.

507
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,880
It's on Yuning's lower part.

508
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,200
(Key suspect)

509
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,419
Unlikely to be the upper one.

510
00:18:18,419 --> 00:18:19,640
It's already moved up.

511
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,464
What do you say, guys?

512
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:24,681
(Who to choose)

513
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,840
I guess it's on Liu Yuning.

514
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:28,280
Yeah.

515
00:18:29,362 --> 00:18:31,019
(Observation team's choice: Yuning)

516
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,520
I only know one dance move.

517
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:37,600
Come on, Xingxu.

518
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:48,480
Okay.

519
00:18:50,616 --> 00:18:51,186
(Empty)

520
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,441
What?

521
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:54,880
What?

522
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,320
What about the top?

523
00:18:57,791 --> 00:18:59,288
(There's a sticker)

524
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:00,840
It's there.

525
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:01,880
Yes, it's on him.

526
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:02,880
On me.

527
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:05,600
(Observation team guessed correctly)
Impressive.

528
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:10,920
Okay, your turn.

529
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:11,880
Come on.

530
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:12,520
Let's discuss.

531
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:15,520
Let me check out the pattern first.

532
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:16,520
Find the smallest one.

533
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:17,160
(Tactics from the start)
Find the smallest one.

534
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,240
This...

535
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:18,680
This one is small.

536
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:21,440
Who do we stick it on?

537
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:23,520
I think they'll definitely guess me.

538
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:24,920
So just don't put it on me.

539
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,360
No, they won't guess you.

540
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:27,560
They won't guess me?

541
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,800
Just like they didn't dare
put it on Chaoyue earlier.

542
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,080
Do you have a tell?

543
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:32,400
I have a little.

544
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:34,160
If you have a tell,
we can't put it on you.

545
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,924
Right, I definitely have a tell.

546
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:36,840
What do we do?

547
00:19:37,143 --> 00:19:37,688
(Who should we put it on?)

548
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,360
I'll act like I have a tell.

549
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,600
We all act nervous.

550
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:42,160
Don't relax.

551
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:42,480
We'll all be like,

552
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,440
"What should I do?

553
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:44,480
It's killing me.

554
00:19:44,480 --> 00:19:45,000
So panicked."

555
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:45,480
Okay?

556
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:46,280
Yeah.

557
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,000
(Hider: Secret
Start acting immediately)

558
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,520
So nervous.

559
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,960
Look, Xingxu keeps his back to us.

560
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:54,840
He's definitely faking.

561
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:55,800
(Already have a target)
Right.

562
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,524
But sometimes, it could be him,

563
